{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Iron and copper are your bars.</b> For in his portion there will be mountains of iron and copper." "<b>And as your days, your דבאך.</b> It has no parallel, and the reason of the translator is known: your strength shall be all your days. And some say the alef stands in place of a doubled letter's letter, like אֲשֶׁר בָּזְאוּ נַהֲרֵי אַרְצוֹ, and the meaning is from the root of דּוֹבֵב שִׂפְתֵי יְשֵׁנִים. And this explanation is without reason."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:37.519227567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}